# Sanity Catalog Migration Scope Contract

## Phase 1: Exact Extraction (The Lead Domino)
Scope Contract: Extract inventory from Sanity via PowerShell into a strict, zero-waste JSON array containing only _id, title, brand, and catalogueLocationKeys.

- Structure:
  - [x] Define GROQ projection: *[_type == "product"]{_id, "title": name, brand, catalogueLocationKeys}
- Logic:
  - [x] Write extract-inventory.ps1 to execute the GROQ query via Sanity CLI.
  - [x] Implement a data sanitation pass in PowerShell to strip any objects containing null values for the projected fields.
- Output:
  - [x] Save output strictly as raw-inventory.json.
  - [x] Assert raw-inventory.json contains zero keys other than _id, title, brand, and catalogueLocationKeys.

## Phase 2: Blueprint Integration & AI Mapping
Scope Contract: Produce a fully nested JSON payload matching the exact recursive structure of data.ts, injecting an array of productIds only at the designated leaf nodes.

- Input:
  - [x] Provide raw-inventory.json and data.ts to the LLM.
  - [x] Define the output schema: The exact JSON representation of data.ts, preserving all _key, _type, title, type, slug, and children fields.
  - [x] Define the mapping rule: Add a new property "productIds": string[] strictly to objects where type == "link".
- Execution:
  - [x] Execute AI processing to map product _ids to the appropriate leaf nodes based on catalogueLocationKeys.
- Output:
  - [x] Save the generated recursive JSON object as nested-catalog-payload.json.

## Phase 3: Structural Validation Assertions
Scope Contract: Programmatically verify the referential integrity of product IDs and the topological integrity of the nested payload using PowerShell.

- Setup:
  - [x] Create test-payload-topology.ps1.
- Logic:
  - [x] Traverse nested-catalog-payload.json recursively.
  - [x] Assert every object where type == "link" contains a "slug" object.
  - [x] Assert every object where type == "link" contains a "productIds" array.
  - [x] Assert every object where type == "header" contains a "children" array and lacks a "productIds" array.
  - [x] Assert every string inside any "productIds" array exists in raw-inventory.json.
- Verification:
  - [x] Test suite exits with code 0.
  - [ ] Test suite must exit with code 0 before Phase 4 can begin.

## Phase 4: Direct Database Mutation
Scope Contract: Safely write the validated, structurally perfect nested payload into Sanity.

- Structure:
  - [x] Write insert-catalog.ps1 to wrap nested-catalog-payload.json in the required Sanity document mutation envelope.
- Logic:
  - [x] Execute Phase 3 test-payload-topology.ps1 as a blocking pre-flight check.
  - [x] Execute Sanity CLI mutation to create or replace the catalog document.
- Verification:
  - [x] Query the new document via GROQ to confirm the nested structure and references resolve correctly.